{"author":{"id":"2462ded6f56967dde059994c39a506c79e39e5dfd10c5a07f07a23a5652a8353"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1775511094,"nonce":"KzaNsXoYq5qGUKYROmTQQt7NJ3s=","title":"Remove @@MARKER@@ instructions from prompts, keep parser as fallback","message":"Remove @@MARKER@@ instructions from prompts, keep parser as fallback\n\n## Context\nSignal protocol Phase 5: once MCP signals (Claude Code, Codex) and file signals (OpenHands, weak models) are in place, remove @@DONE@@/@@CHECKPOINT@@/@@QUESTION@@/@@WAITING@@ text instructions from prompts. Keep parse_marker() in core/protocols.py for backward compatibility with old sessions.\n\nDepends on: 91a18ed (Claude Code MCP), 7cb8425 (Codex MCP), b16bb9b (OpenHands file signals)\n\n## Tests (write first, must fail before implementation)\n- tests/test_prompts.py::test_prompt_does_not_contain_at_markers\n  Assert: rendered WORKFLOW.md prompt for all agent kinds does NOT contain \"@@DONE@@\" or \"@@CHECKPOINT@@\" or \"@@QUESTION@@\" or \"@@WAITING@@\"\n- tests/test_marker_reliability.py::test_parse_marker_still_works_for_legacy\n  Assert: parse_marker(\"@@DONE@@\") still returns DONE (backward compat)\n\n## Files\n- templates/WORKFLOW.md (modify — remove @@MARKER@@ instruction sections)\n- core/protocols.py (keep parse_marker unchanged — backward compat)\n\n## Implementation\n1. In templates/WORKFLOW.md, remove any sections instructing the agent to output @@DONE@@, @@CHECKPOINT@@, @@QUESTION@@, or @@WAITING@@ text markers.\n2. Do NOT remove parse_marker() from core/protocols.py — it must remain for parsing old session logs and as a last-resort fallback.\n3. Do NOT remove marker handling from adapter _parse() methods — they still emit marker-style events internally.\n\n## Patterns to follow\nSee templates/WORKFLOW.md for current marker instructions.\n\n## Notes\n- This is the final cleanup step. All signal detection now goes through MCP tools or file signals.\n- Text markers may still appear in agent output (models are trained on them). The parsers handle them silently.\n- Template version should be bumped (major bump — behavioral change).\n\nREQ: REQ-004","files":null}]}